---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="40–45 min" data-extension-duration="10–15 min">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson 07</p>
  <h1>Question words: <em>what, where, who, how</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Four small words help open many basic conversations. Use <span class="ex">what</span> for a thing, <span class="ex">where</span> for a place, <span class="ex">who</span> for a person, and <span class="ex">how</span> for a feeling or a way. Then keep the order simple: <strong>question word + <em>be</em> + subject</strong>.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 40–45 min</span>
    <span class="tag">what / where / who / how</span>
    <span class="tag">with <em>be</em></span>
    <span class="tag">answer type → question</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Read an answer, find its question.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Each word asks for one category.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Match, choose, and build questions.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Meet, ask, and make small talk.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">We stay with the verb <span class="ex">be</span> here: <span class="ex">am / is / are</span>. You already use it. Now you put a question word in front of it.</p>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>An answer, then its question</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">What is your job? &nbsp; I'm a nurse.</span><br /><span class="ex">Where are you from? &nbsp; I'm from Peru.</span><br /><span class="ex">Who is that? &nbsp; That's my manager.</span><br /><span class="ex">How are you? &nbsp; Fine, thanks.</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>One answer is a <strong>thing</strong>, one is a <strong>place</strong>, one is a <strong>person</strong>, and one is a <strong>feeling</strong>. Which question word goes with each?</li>
      <li>Look at the order of every question. Which word comes <strong>first</strong>? Which word comes <strong>second</strong>?</li>
      <li>So if you know what kind of answer you want, you can pick the question word. What kind of answer does <span class="ex">where</span> ask for?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. The answers identify a place for Where, job information for What, a person for Who, and a feeling for How.">
    <h3>Discovery check: read the answer, then choose the question word</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">The answer in brackets is the cue. What kind of thing is it: a thing, a place, a person, or a feeling?</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="What">What</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Where">Where</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Who">Who</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="How">How</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Where" data-hint="The answer gives a country, which is a place." data-fix="Where are you from?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> are you from? &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(Answer: I'm from Peru.)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="What" data-hint="The answer gives job information, not a person’s identity." data-fix="What is your job?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> is your job? &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(Answer: I'm a teacher.)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Who" data-hint="The answer identifies a person." data-fix="Who is that?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> is that? &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(Answer: That's my boss.)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="How" data-hint="The answer describes a feeling or condition." data-fix="How are you today?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> are you today? &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(Answer: Fine, thanks.)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: one word, one category</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Each question word asks for one kind of answer. Decide the kind first, then the word is easy:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>question word</th><th>it asks about</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>what</b></td><td>a thing or information</td><td><span class="contraction">What is your name?</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>where</b></td><td>a place</td><td><span class="contraction">Where is the office?</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>who</b></td><td>a person</td><td><span class="contraction">Who is that?</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>how</b></td><td>a feeling or a way</td><td><span class="contraction">How are you?</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>Then the word order stays the same every time:</p>
  <p><strong>question word + <em>be</em> + subject</strong></p>
  <p><span class="ex">Where &nbsp;·&nbsp; are &nbsp;·&nbsp; you</span> &nbsp;→&nbsp; <span class="ex">Where are you from?</span><br /><span class="ex">What &nbsp;·&nbsp; is &nbsp;·&nbsp; your job</span> &nbsp;→&nbsp; <span class="ex">What is your job?</span></p>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>This pattern is for <em>be</em></h3>
    <p>Use this lesson’s order when the verb is <span class="ex">am, is,</span> or <span class="ex">are</span>: <span class="ex">Where is the office?</span> Do not add <span class="ex">be</span> before an action word such as <span class="ex">work</span>: not <span class="ex">Where are you work?</span> The natural question is <span class="ex">Where do you work?</span>, a later question pattern.</p>
    <p><span class="ex">What is your job?</span> is clear. In everyday U.S. English, people also often ask <span class="ex">What do you do?</span> You will learn that action-verb pattern with the present simple.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Meaning check</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Can we say <span class="ex">Who are you from?</span> for a place? <strong>No.</strong> <em>Who</em> asks about a person. For a place we say <span class="ex">Where are you from?</span></li>
      <li>When you meet someone and want the person to tell you their name, ask <span class="ex">What is your name?</span> The question <span class="ex">Where is your name?</span> asks about the location of a written name.</li>
      <li>What does <span class="ex">How are you?</span> ask for? A <strong>feeling</strong> or condition, not a place. The answer is <span class="ex">Fine, thanks.</span> or <span class="ex">I'm tired.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Useful fixed questions</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Keep these whole. They open most first conversations:</p>
  <p><span class="ex">What's your name? &nbsp; · &nbsp; Where are you from?</span><br /><span class="ex">Who is that woman? &nbsp; · &nbsp; How are you? Fine, thanks.</span></p>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Sound natural: say the question as one complete thought</h3>
    <p>Link the question word to <span class="ex">is</span> or <span class="ex">are</span>. Make the information you want clear, and let your voice fall gently at the end.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>question</th><th>natural rhythm</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>What is your name?</td><td>What’s your <b>NAME</b>?</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Where are you from?</td><td>Where-are-you <b>FROM</b>?</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Who is that?</td><td>Who-is <b>THAT</b>?</td></tr>
        <tr><td>How are you?</td><td>How-are-<b>YOU</b>?</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>These questions ask for information, so they usually end with a falling voice, not the rising voice of many yes/no questions. Notice that <span class="ex">who</span> begins with an <em>h</em> sound; the written <em>w</em> is silent.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="thinking-card" data-lesson-extension="Optional tutor-read intonation contrast">
    <h3>Listen for the question type</h3>
    <p>Look away from the script. Your tutor reads each pair. Say “information” for the question with <span class="ex">what</span> or <span class="ex">where</span>, and “yes or no” for the other question. Then repeat the information question with a gentle fall.</p>
    <details>
      <summary>Tutor script and listening key</summary>
      <ol>
        <li><span class="ex">What is your name?</span> (information, falling) · <span class="ex">Is your name Ana?</span> (yes or no, often rising)</li>
        <li><span class="ex">Where is the meeting?</span> (information, falling) · <span class="ex">Is the meeting upstairs?</span> (yes or no, often rising)</li>
      </ol>
    </details>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. Each short answer makes the missing information type clear: information, place, person, or condition.">
    <h3>Drill 1: choose the question word</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Read the short answer in brackets. It tells you a thing, a place, a person, or a feeling.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="What">What</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Where">Where</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Who">Who</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="How">How</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="What" data-hint="The answer gives number information." data-fix="What is your phone number?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> is your phone number? <span class="contraction">(Answer: It's 555-0199.)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Where" data-hint="Room 3 is a place." data-fix="Where is the meeting?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> is the meeting? <span class="contraction">(Answer: In room 3.)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Who" data-hint="Mr. Diaz identifies a person." data-fix="Who is your teacher?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> is your teacher? <span class="contraction">(Answer: Mr. Diaz.)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="How" data-hint="Well describes a person’s condition." data-fix="How is your mother?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> is your mother? <span class="contraction">(Answer: She's well, thanks.)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Where" data-hint="At lunch gives the colleagues’ location." data-fix="Where are your colleagues?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> are your colleagues? <span class="contraction">(Answer: At lunch.)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="What" data-hint="Romano gives name information, not a location." data-fix="What is your last name?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> is your last name? <span class="contraction">(Answer: It's Romano.)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the meaning, then the question</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-game data-lesson-extension="Optional information-type matching" data-success-message="Correct. What asks for information, where for a place, who for a person, and how for a condition or way.">
    <h3>Drill 2: match each word to what it asks about</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Tap a question word, then tap the meaning that fits it</p>
    <div class="tile-bank">
      <button class="tile" data-tile="what">what</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="where">where</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="who">who</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="how">how</button>
    </div>
    <div class="slot-board">
      <button class="slot" data-slot="what" data-hint="Use this word for a name, number, thing, or other information." data-fix="what → a thing or information" data-placeholder="a thing or information">a thing or information</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="where" data-hint="Use this word when the answer is a location." data-fix="where → a place" data-placeholder="a place">a place</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="who" data-hint="Use this word when the answer identifies a person." data-fix="who → a person" data-placeholder="a person">a person</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="how" data-hint="Use this word for a condition, feeling, or way." data-fix="how → a feeling or a way" data-placeholder="a feeling or a way">a feeling or a way</button>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-tiles>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-tiles>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="where are you from" data-hint="Begin with the place question word, then put are before you." data-fix="Where are you from?" data-success-message="Correct. The question asks for a place, and are comes before the subject you.">
    <h3>Drill 3: build the question</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">You meet someone new and want their country. Build the question, then say it.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="you">you</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="where">Where</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="from">from</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="are">are</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="what is your job" data-hint="Begin with the information question word, then put is before your job." data-fix="What is your job?" data-success-message="Correct. The question asks for job information, and is comes before the subject phrase your job.">
    <h3>Drill 4: build the question</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">You want to know the person's work. Build the question.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="job">job</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="what">What</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="your">your</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="is">is</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="how are you today" data-hint="Begin with the condition question word, then put are before you." data-fix="How are you today?" data-success-message="Correct. How asks about the listener’s condition, and are comes before you.">
    <h3>Drill 5: build the question</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">You greet a coworker in the morning. Build the question.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="today">today</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="how">How</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="you">you</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="are">are</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="who" data-hint="The answer is a country, so check whether the first word asks for a place." data-fix="Where are you from?" data-why="From asks for a place, so use where, not who. Who asks about a person.">
    <h3>Drill 6: fix the question word</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong. The answer is a country.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="who">Who</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="are">are</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="you">you</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="from">from?</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="where" data-hint="The answer gives name information, not the location of written text." data-fix="What is your name?" data-why="A name is information, so use “what,” not “where.” “Where” asks for a place.">
    <h3>Drill 7: fix the question word</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong. The answer is a name.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="where">Where</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="is">is</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="your">your</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="name">name?</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform data-lesson-extension="Optional answer-to-question oral recall">
    <h3>Drill 8: read the answer, then say the question</h3>
    <p>The answer is given. Say the question aloud first. Reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> I'm from Brazil. &nbsp;→&nbsp; ask for the place</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Where are you from?</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> I'm an engineer. &nbsp;→&nbsp; ask for the job</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>What is your job?</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> He's my brother. &nbsp;→&nbsp; ask about the person</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Who is that?</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> Fine, thanks. &nbsp;→&nbsp; ask about the feeling</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>How are you?</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> My name is Ana. &nbsp;→&nbsp; ask for the name</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>What is your name?</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>First introductions:</b> Imagine you just met someone at a conference. Ask all four questions in order: <span class="ex">What's your name? &nbsp; Where are you from? &nbsp; What is your job? &nbsp; How are you?</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Point and ask:</b> Look at a photo of people (real or invented). For each person, ask the teacher: <span class="ex">Who is that?</span> Then give the answer.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Lost in a new city:</b> You need a place. Ask the teacher for directions to three places: <span class="ex">Where is the station? &nbsp; Where is the hotel? &nbsp; Where is the bank?</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Small talk at work:</b> Greet a coworker and keep it going. <span class="ex">How are you today?</span> &nbsp;<span class="ex">Fine, thanks. And you?</span> Then ask one more question with <em>what</em> or <em>where</em>.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Information gap:</b> Your teacher gives one short answer at a time about a thing, a place, a person, or a feeling. Ask the matching complete question without seeing the teacher’s question card. Switch roles and repeat.</div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Success check</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Ask one clear question with each of the four question words.</li>
      <li>Match the question word to the answer type you need.</li>
      <li>Put <span class="ex">am, is,</span> or <span class="ex">are</span> before the subject.</li>
      <li>Say each information question as one thought with a gentle fall.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the choice</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “I use <strong>what</strong> for a ______. I use <strong>where</strong> for a ______. I use <strong>who</strong> for a ______. I use <strong>how</strong> for a ______. In every question, the order is question word, then ______, then the subject.”</p>
    <p>Then ask the teacher one true question with each of the four words.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Excellent. You can choose what, where, who, or how by the kind of answer you want, and keep the word order with be.">
    <h3>Final quiz: choose the right question word</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="where" data-hint="Mexico is a place." data-fix="Where are you from?">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. (Answer: I'm from Mexico.) ___ are you from?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="what">what</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="where">where</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="who">who</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="how">how</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="what" data-hint="Doctor gives job information." data-fix="What is your job?">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. (Answer: I'm a doctor.) ___ is your job?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="what">what</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="where">where</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="who">who</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="how">how</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="who" data-hint="The answer identifies a person." data-fix="Who is that?">
